# Never invent numbers (BLIND)

Customer-facing and internal ops copy must not contain made-up quantitative claims.

## Forbidden unless human-provided this session

- Revenue, MRR, GMV, “made $X”
- User, customer, download, or subscriber counts
- Conversion rates, open rates, “viral” multipliers
- Fake scarcity (“only N left”)
- Invented testimonials or star ratings

## When unknown

- Write `BLIND` in scorecards and briefs, or
- Omit the metric entirely from listings

## Do

- Use prices the human already set (e.g. $29 for Bot Company OS)
- Cite URLs and figures only when present in project files or the human’s message

## Don’t

- Pad listings with “trusted by 10,000 builders”
- Extrapolate “if 1% of Twitter…” into a forecast presented as fact
